# Pixelanea Frontend Antipatterns

Stack: **React 19**, **Zustand 5**, **Vite**, generated **OpenAPI client**, **Radix** primitives.

Symptom of many of these: **blank or black screen** with no UI — React crashes before paint.

## Zustand selectors

Never return a **new object or array** from a selector without shallow compare. React 19 + Zustand will infinite-loop (`Maximum update depth exceeded`, `getSnapshot should be cached`).

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — new object every snapshot → blank screen
useUiStore((s) => ({ status: s.apiStatus, version: s.apiVersion }));

// ✅ GOOD — primitive or stable reference
const status = useUiStore((s) => s.apiStatus);
const version = useUiStore((s) => s.apiVersion);

// ✅ GOOD — multi-field object with useShallow
useUiStore(useShallow((s) => ({ status: s.apiStatus, version: s.apiVersion })));
```

Same rule for arrays: `useStore((s) => s.items.filter(...))` needs `useShallow` or a memoized selector.

**Prefer:** one primitive per selector, or `useShallow` for tuples/objects.

## React state & effects

- **No `setState` / store updates during render** — only in event handlers or effects.
- **Stable effect deps** — don't pass inline objects/arrays to `useEffect` deps; extract primitives.
- **Don't subscribe to the whole store** — `useStore()` without a selector re-renders on every change.

## Layer boundaries (see `pixelanea-frontend.mdc`)

| Anti-pattern | Fix |
|--------------|-----|
| `fetch('/api/...')` or hand-rolled DTOs in components | `api/` wrappers + `@pixelanea/api-client` |
| Store imports in `components/ui/` | Pass props/callbacks from shell or feature components |
| Canvas coordinate math outside `canvas/` | Keep grid math in `canvas/` only |
| User-facing strings inline in JSX | `content/` copy maps |

## Browser / theme

- **`window` / `document` in module scope** — breaks SSR/tests; use effects or guarded helpers.
- **Theme class** — apply via `applyThemeToDocument` in bootstrap effect, not only on toggle.

## Review checklist

- [ ] Store selectors return primitives, or use `useShallow`
- [ ] No new object/array literals in selectors without shallow compare
- [ ] API calls go through `apps/web/src/api/`
- [ ] UI still paints after change (no empty `#root`)
